From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChristosNtokos <chrisdokos1@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rtl8822ce: log a TX DMA error and dump the TX rings once per
 error

xmit_status_check() runs every 2 s. While REG_TXDMA_STATUS is
non-zero, it printks the whole TX ring backup (core_get_tx_ring_ext(),
about 700 lines) on every run. With the silent reset compiled out,
the error never cleared: about 11 MB of journal a minute, which pushed
every older log out of a 500 MB journal within an hour.

Print one warning line with the register value and the ring dump only
on the first check that sees the error. When a later check reads zero
again, print one line saying it cleared, and log the next error in
full. Both lines bypass the driver's log level (0 by default, which
hides RTW_INFO), so a reset and its outcome stay visible.

The flag is initialised only in sreset_init_value(), not in
sreset_reset_value(): the silent reset itself calls
sreset_reset_value() through rtw_reset_drv_sw(), and clearing the flag
there would bring back a dump on every check while resets keep failing.

Unchanged: the per-frame check in rtl8822ce_xmit.c still dumps once,
at the first error after the module loads, and freezes the backup
(DUMP_TXBD_HALT). So the first error can print two dumps, and a later
error's dump repeats the frames of the first one.
'echo "1 1" > /proc/net/rtl88x2ce/wlan0/tx_ring_ext' re-arms the backup.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: ChristosNtokos <chrisdokos1@gmail.com>
---
 .../realtek/rtl8822ce/core/rtw_sreset.c        |  1 +
 .../rtl8822ce/hal/rtl8822c/rtl8822c_ops.c      | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../realtek/rtl8822ce/include/rtw_sreset.h     |  1 +
 3 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/core/rtw_sreset.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/core/rtw_sreset.c
index 21cc18b..d84b879 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/core/rtw_sreset.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/core/rtw_sreset.c
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ void sreset_init_value(_adapter *padapter)
 	psrtpriv->Wifi_Error_Status = WIFI_STATUS_SUCCESS;
 	psrtpriv->last_tx_time = 0;
 	psrtpriv->last_tx_complete_time = 0;
+	psrtpriv->txdma_err_logged = _FALSE;
 #endif
 }
 void sreset_reset_value(_adapter *padapter)
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/hal/rtl8822c/rtl8822c_ops.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/hal/rtl8822c/rtl8822c_ops.c
index bde359c..0c51386 100755
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/hal/rtl8822c/rtl8822c_ops.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/hal/rtl8822c/rtl8822c_ops.c
@@ -1038,11 +1038,27 @@ static void xmit_status_check(PADAPTER p)
 	if (txdma_status != 0x00) {
 		RTW_INFO("%s REG_TXDMA_STATUS:0x%08x\n", __FUNCTION__, txdma_status);
 
-		core_get_tx_ring_ext(p);
+		/*
+		 * Log the error and dump the TX rings (~700 lines) once per
+		 * error, not on every 2 s check for as long as it lasts.
+		 */
+		if (!psrtpriv->txdma_err_logged) {
+			psrtpriv->txdma_err_logged = _TRUE;
+			printk(KERN_WARNING DRIVER_PREFIX FUNC_ADPT_FMT
+			       ": TX DMA error, REG_TXDMA_STATUS=0x%08x, resetting\n",
+			       FUNC_ADPT_ARG(p), txdma_status);
+			core_get_tx_ring_ext(p);
+		}
 
 		psrtpriv->tx_dma_status_cnt++;
 		psrtpriv->self_dect_case = 4;
 		rtw_hal_sreset_reset(p);
+	} else if (psrtpriv->txdma_err_logged) {
+		psrtpriv->txdma_err_logged = _FALSE;
+		printk(KERN_INFO DRIVER_PREFIX FUNC_ADPT_FMT
+		       ": TX DMA error cleared, %llu TX DMA resets since load\n",
+		       FUNC_ADPT_ARG(p),
+		       (unsigned long long)psrtpriv->tx_dma_status_cnt);
 	}
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB_HCI
 	current_time = rtw_get_current_time();
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/include/rtw_sreset.h b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/include/rtw_sreset.h
index 1fd999a..0f46c89 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/include/rtw_sreset.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/include/rtw_sreset.h
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ struct sreset_priv {
 	u8 self_dect_case;
 	u16 last_mac_rxff_ptr;
 	u8 dbg_sreset_ctrl;
+	u8 txdma_err_logged;	/* this TX DMA error was already logged */
 };
 
 
